From 52249b304f4681f5532ac5dd53ec0679aae7baeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 07:38:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] LocalDisplayAdapter: pre-set state and committedState to ON
 for first internal display

On devices where the vendor HWC does not implement getDisplayConnectionType
(e.g. HIDL HWC 2.1 as shipped on many MediaTek devices), SurfaceFlinger
powers on the built-in display during its own initialisation, before
LocalDisplayAdapter exists.  Both mState and mCommittedState are initialised
to STATE_UNKNOWN and stay there until the first requestDisplayStateLocked
call from DisplayPowerController, which only arrives after system_server has
fully booted -- potentially hours into first boot due to dex optimisation.

During this window:
- DisplayManagerService.getDisplayInfo(0) returns null because LogicalDisplay
  treats STATE_UNKNOWN as 'not ready', causing:
  PowerManagerService: 'Tried to acquire wake lock for invalid display: 0'
  -- the screen goes dark as soon as the boot animation exits
- Touch ICs gated on DRM notifier callbacks (e.g. chipone_tddi via
  tct_display_touch_interface) interpret STATE_UNKNOWN as display-off and
  suspend themselves -- touch is dead until state is committed
- DeviceStateManagerService stalls: 'Cannot notify device state info change
  before the initial state has been committed'

The fix: for the first internal display, initialise both mState and
mCommittedState to STATE_ON at construction time, then call
updateDeviceInfoLocked() to propagate the values into mInfo immediately.
SurfaceFlinger always powers on the primary display before LocalDisplayAdapter
is created, so STATE_ON reflects physical reality.  The subsequent
requestDisplayStateLocked call will update both fields normally.
---
 .../server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java   | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
index 6865a23a7..5885e905b 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
@@ -276,6 +276,26 @@ final class LocalDisplayAdapter extends DisplayAdapter {
             mBacklightAdapter = mInjector.getBacklightAdapter(displayToken, isFirstDisplay,
                     mSurfaceControlProxy);
             mActiveSfDisplayModeAtStartId = dynamicInfo.activeDisplayModeId;
+
+            // On devices where the vendor HWC does not implement getDisplayConnectionType
+            // (e.g. HIDL HWC 2.1), SurfaceFlinger powers on the built-in display during
+            // its own init before LocalDisplayAdapter exists.  Both mState and mCommittedState
+            // stay at STATE_UNKNOWN until the first requestDisplayStateLocked call, which only
+            // arrives after system_server has fully booted.  During that window:
+            // - DisplayManagerService.getDisplayInfo(0) returns null (mInfo.state is UNKNOWN)
+            //   because the LogicalDisplay is not considered valid
+            // - PowerManagerService cannot acquire a wake lock for display 0 and returns early,
+            //   so the screen goes dark immediately after the boot animation ends
+            // - Touch ICs gated on DRM notifier state (e.g. chipone_tddi via
+            //   tct_display_touch_interface) keep themselves suspended
+            // Pre-set both fields to STATE_ON for the first internal display to reflect the
+            // physical reality: SurfaceFlinger already powered it on.  Call
+            // updateDeviceInfoLocked() to propagate into mInfo immediately.
+            if (isFirstDisplay && staticDisplayInfo.isInternal) {
+                mState = Display.STATE_ON;
+                mCommittedState = Display.STATE_ON;
+                updateDeviceInfoLocked();
+            }
         }
 
         @Override
